9	MDCAT 2017	mdcat-2017	2017	f	t	2026-08-11 19:44:53.251654+05	1	220 official MCQs total (UHS Lahore, Entrance Test 2017). 216 active+verified in DB. Chemistry #55-58 (paper question numbers 217-220) are permanently unrecoverable: recorded as illegible in the original scan by two independent sources — our own OCR-based transcription AND a separately compiled answer key (mdcat_2017_alternate.pdf, 'Compiled By: NOOR MOBIN', held locally in media/source_checks/) both mark these as 'X'/blank with no readable question text. Not a gap in our pipeline — the source itself has nothing to recover here. If a cleaner scan of this paper's Chemistry questions 55-58 ever surfaces, these can be added.\n\nAlso note: questions 128, 132, and 209 (paper_order set) were added with an independently-derived answer since UHS's own key left them unresolved too — see the '[Note: ...]' text appended to each of those three questions for the reasoning.	This paper has 216 of the original 220 questions. The last 4 (Chemistry) were illegible in every copy of the original paper we checked, so they're left out rather than guessed at.
11	MDCAT 2015	mdcat-2015	2015	f	t	2026-08-11 22:39:01.9536+05	1	Full pass (Aug 2026) against learnospot.com/uhs-mdcat-past-paper-5 (independent full-paper transcription) plus direct chemistry/physics/biology verification and viewing the 6 already-attached source images. Went from 192 to 217 active+verified.\n\n7 answer-key corrections (see prior note) + reconstructed/decoded 5 more from genuinely garbled OCR text where the underlying content was still recoverable (1865 dipeptide stem rewritten from decoded atoms + cross-confirmed against learnospot; 1893 IUPAC name decoded from structure fragments; 1896 SN2 mechanism decoded, textbook inversion confirms answer; 2035 'inhibits'->'stimulates' corrected, independently verified secretin stimulates pancreatic secretion; 1868 zwitterion reconstructed as the standard 4 protonation states of an amino acid, the canonical option set for this question type — correct option confirmed by a surviving text fragment).\n\n3 remain inactive, and unlike the above, these are NOT being reconstructed because the missing information is positional/relational, not just badly formatted — there is no single well-defined 'standard' way to fill the gap without guessing:\n- Q1902 (alpha-carbon): needs to know which drawn carbon was numbered '1' vs '2' vs '3' vs '4' in the original diagram — arbitrary per-diagram, not recoverable from text.\n- Q1967 (food-web trophic level): needs the actual arrows/who-eats-whom relationships; a jumbled species list carries no relational information to reconstruct from.\n- Q1900 (DNPH product): the correct chemical product IS knowable (acetaldehyde's 2,4-dinitrophenylhydrazone), but the 3 wrong options have no canonical standard form the way 1868's did — could have been a wrong reagent, wrong carbonyl, wrong stoichiometry, etc. — too open-ended to responsibly reconstruct.	This paper has 217 of the original 220 questions. The remaining 3 (one Biology food-web question, two Chemistry structure questions) each need information from the original diagram that we could not recover from any available source, so they're left out rather than guessed at.
16	MDCAT 2012	mdcat-2012	2012	f	t	2026-08-18 23:09:11.734066+05	1	Full paper-wide answer verification pass (2026-08-20). The original OCR/parsing pipeline (mdcat_2012.py) read the exam's two-column option layout (A/C printed side-by-side on line 1, B/D on line 2) in raster order, silently swapping options B and C for the large majority of text-only questions across the whole paper. correct_answer was derived by pairing the official key (correct, real-paper letters) directly against these swapped option lists, corrupting the answer whenever the correct choice was B or C -- including on rows already marked is_verified. Re-verified every one of the 219 active questions against the officially transcribed 2012 UHS answer key (mdcatguide.com scan, key page transcribed to mdcat-content/tmp_2012/official_key_2012.json) using content-based option matching (not letter position), independently confirmed each fix against subject-matter reasoning, and fixed 88 wrong correct_answer values (66 of which were already marked is_verified=True). Source mdcat-content/parsed-mcqs/MDCAT_2012.json updated in lockstep (needs_review cleared) so a future re-run of scripts/convert_2012_to_json.py from mdcat_2012.py will not reintroduce these errors -- note mdcat_2012.py itself still has the underlying option-order bug, only the derived JSON/DB were corrected. Two questions (Q147 gastrin, Q213 oxygenated-blood vein) have no option-order issue but the official key still disagrees with clear science; DB kept at the scientifically correct answer (B for both) -- see each question's own notes for details. Paper now 219/219 active, 219/219 verified.	
