2154	Choose the CORRECT sentence:	The government introduced tax laws which gave incentives to factory workers to reduce pollution.	The government introduced tax laws who gave incentives to factory workers to reduce pollution.	The government introduced tax laws which have incentives to factory workers to reduce pollution.	The government introduced tax laws which has incentives to factory workers to reduce pollution.	A	medium	'Which gave' is correct: 'which' refers to the inanimate noun 'tax laws,' and 'gave' (plural-agreeing) matches 'laws.'	Since 'tax laws' are things (not people), the relative pronoun must be 'which,' not 'who.' Additionally, the verb must agree with the plural subject 'tax laws,' making 'gave' correct rather than the singular 'has'/'have' mismatches in the other options.	Use 'which' for things, 'who' for people; and check subject-verb agreement in the relative clause.	2026-08-18 16:22:35.565367+05	t	2026-08-12 01:54:47.977471+05	2026-08-18 16:22:35.565641+05	12	284	t	f	\N	{"a": "Correct — 'which' correctly refers to 'tax laws,' and 'gave' matches the plural subject.", "b": "'Who' incorrectly treats 'tax laws' as if they were people.", "c": "'Have incentives' shifts to present tense inconsistently and describes existence rather than the action of giving.", "d": "'Has incentives' is both a tense mismatch and a subject-verb agreement error (laws is plural, 'has' is singular)."}
